 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "SquirrelResearch() tracks locations by id; an unseen location is empty. Level i has capacity F(i + 2) (1, 2, 3, 5, 8, ...). hideNuts(locationId, count) places nuts greedily from the deepest level upward, filling each level before the next, and returns the highest non-empty level index (-1 if the location is empty). retrieveNuts(locationId, count) removes min(count, stored) nuts from the highest levels downward and returns how many were removed. getHighestLevel(locationId) returns the highest non-empty level or -1. Because filling is bottom-up and removal top-down, the occupied levels always form a prefix. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "be5d798382a43847401e76609d79932746e664be0d91c81b132bf6b46cd69126",
    "selector": "/problems/30/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
